  "files": [
    {
      "path": "index.html",
      "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n  <title>Pixel Calculator</title>\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n</head>\n<body>\n  <main class=\"card\">\n    <h1>Pixel Calculator</h1>\n    <div class=\"field\">\n      <label for=\"left\">Left number</label>\n      <input type=\"number\" id=\"left\" step=\"any\" placeholder=\"e.g. 5\">\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"field\">\n      <label for=\"operation\">Operation</label>\n      <select id=\"operation\">\n        <option value=\"add\">Add</option>\n        <option value=\"subtract\">Subtract</option>\n        <option value=\"multiply\">Multiply</option>\n        <option value=\"divide\">Divide</option>\n      </select>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"field\">\n      <label for=\"right\">Right number</label>\n      <input type=\"number\" id=\"right\" step=\"any\" placeholder=\"e.g. 3\">\n    </div>\n    <button id=\"calculate\">Calculate</button>\n    <output id=\"result\" for=\"left operation right\">0</output>\n  </main>\n  <script src=\"script.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "description": ""
    },
    {
      "path": "style.css",
      "content": "/* Pixel-style calculator - cohesive 4-color palette */\n:root {\n  --bg: #1a1c2c;\n  --card: #2d2f45;\n  --accent: #ffcd75;\n  --text: #f4f4f4;\n  --border: #5a5e7a;\n  --shadow: #0f101a;\n}\n\n* { box-sizing: border-box; }\n\nbody {\n  margin: 0;\n  min-height: 100vh;\n  display: grid;\n  place-items: center;\n  background: var(--bg);\n  font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;\n  font-size: 16px;\n  color: var(--text);\n  padding: 16px;\n}\n\n.card {\n  background: var(--card);\n  padding: 24px;\n  border: 4px solid var(--border);\n  box-shadow: 8px 8px 0 var(--shadow);\n  width: min(100%, 400px);\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  gap: 16px;\n}\n\nh1 {\n  margin: 0 0 8px;\n  font-size: 1.5rem;\n  text-align: center;\n  letter-spacing: 1px;\n  color: var(--accent);\n  text-shadow: 2px 2px 0 var(--shadow);\n}\n\n.field {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n  gap: 4px;\n}\n\nlabel {\n  font-size: 0.9rem;\n  font-weight: 600;\n  color: var(--accent);\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  letter-spacing: 0.5px;\n}\n\ninput, select, button {\n  font: inherit;\n  padding: 10px 12px;\n  border: 3px solid var(--border);\n  background: var(--bg);\n  color: var(--text);\n  border-radius: 0;\n  outline: none;\n}\n\ninput:focus, select:focus, button:focus-visible {\n  border-color: var(--accent);\n  box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--accent);\n}\n\ninput:hover, select:hover {\n  border-color: var(--accent);\n}\n\nbutton {\n  cursor: pointer;\n  background: var(--accent);\n  color: var(--bg);\n  font-weight: 700;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  letter-spacing: 1px;\n  transition: transform 0.05s, box-shadow 0.05s;\n  box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--shadow);\n}\n\nbutton:hover {\n  background: #ffe08a;\n}\n\nbutton:active {\n  transform: translate(4px, 4px);\n  box-shadow: 0 0 0 var(--shadow);\n}\n\noutput {\n  display: block;\n  margin-top: 8px;\n  padding: 12px;\n  background: var(--bg);\n  border: 3px solid var(--border);\n  font-size: 1.5rem;\n  font-weight: 700;\n  text-align: right;\n  min-height: 3rem;\n  color: var(--accent);\n  overflow-wrap: anywhere;\n}\n\n@media (max-width: 400px) {\n  .card { padding: 16px; gap: 12px; }\n  h1 { font-size: 1.25rem; }\n  output { font-size: 1.25rem; }\n}",
      "description": ""
    },
    {
      "path": "script.js",
      "content": "const leftInput = document.getElementById('left');\nconst rightInput = document.getElementById('right');\nconst operationSelect = document.getElementById('operation');\nconst calculateBtn = document.getElementById('calculate');\nconst resultOutput = document.getElementById('result');\n\nfunction getNumber(input) {\n  const raw = input.value.trim();\n  if (raw === '') return null;\n  const num = Number(raw);\n  return Number.isFinite(num) ? num : null;\n}\n\nfunction calculate() {\n  const left = getNumber(leftInput);\n  const right = getNumber(rightInput);\n  if (left === null || right === null) {\n    resultOutput.textContent = 'Error';\n    return;\n  }\n\n  const op = operationSelect.value;\n  let result;\n\n  switch (op) {\n    case 'add':\n      result = left + right;\n      break;\n    case 'subtract':\n      result = left - right;\n      break;\n    case 'multiply':\n      result = left * right;\n      break;\n    case 'divide':\n      if (right === 0) {\n        resultOutput.textContent = 'Error';\n        return;\n      }\n      result = left / right;\n      break;\n    default:\n      resultOutput.textContent = 'Error';\n      return;\n  }\n\n  if (!Number.isFinite(result)) {\n    resultOutput.textContent = 'Error';\n    return;\n  }\n\n  resultOutput.textContent = String(result);\n}\n\ncalculateBtn.addEventListener('click', calculate);",
      "description": ""
    },
    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# Pixel Two-Number Calculator\n\nA tiny offline pixel-style calculator built with plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. No packages, no network requests, no storage.\n\n## Features\n\n- Two number inputs (`left`, `right`) with support for negative and decimal values.\n- Operation selector (`operation`) with add, subtract, multiply, and divide.\n- Calculate button (`calculate`) and result output (`result`) that starts at `0`.\n- Output shows only the numeric result (no label).\n- Invalid input (empty or non-finite) and division by zero show exactly `Error`.\n- Keyboard accessible with labeled controls and visible focus/hover/pressed states.\n- Responsive layout that works from 360px wide.\n\n## Usage\n\n1. Open `index.html` in any modern browser.\n2. Enter a number in the left field.\n3. Choose an operation.\n4. Enter a number in the right field.\n5. Click **Calculate** (or focus the button and press Enter/Space).\n6. The result appears in the output box; on invalid input it shows `Error`.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- `index.html` — semantic markup with required IDs and labels.\n- `style.css` — pixel-inspired card, 4-color palette, responsive rules, and interactive states.\n- `script.js` — validation, arithmetic, division-by-zero handling, and event listener.\n\nAll files are local and use relative paths. No external assets or iframes.",
      "description": ""
    }
  ]
